  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1144 PM CDT SAT AUG 8 2026\n\nCentral Alabama remains in a somewhat weak upper flow area south \nof the main broad trough that extends out of Central Canada and \ndown into the Great Lakes. At the same time, Alabama is situated \nbetween two ridges, one across the Four Corners and the other in \nthe Western Atlantic off of the FL Coast along with a weak, small \nshortwave from the main upper trough just to our NW. This will not\nmake a big difference as it propagates EWD across the SE US as it\nremains weak. Our emphasis will still be typical summertime \ndiurnally enhanced convection overall. By Monday, the Western \nAtlantic ridge flattens and retrogrades further westward across \nthe Northern Gulf Coast. At the same time, it also shows the upper\nshortwave absorbed back into the longwave trough with continued \nsummertime diurnally enhanced activity expected through the \nremainder of the week. \n\nAs for temperatures, readings vary only a degree or so here and \nthere through mid week with overall moisture remaining up. This \nwill result in max afternoon heat indices perhaps a couple of \ndegrees higher in spots. However, guidance continues to keep us \nbelow heat advisory criteria for now. We will be watching as we\nhead into the end of the week with a medium chance of the upper \nridge building into and getting stronger across the SE US and \ntemperatures warming further. This could inch us back closer to \nheat advisory criteria by Friday into next weekend.\n\n08",
